This is an error that you do not have the libicui18n C library, which is required by the {stringi} package, which is a deep dependency of poppr.
The author of stringi has provided instructions for installing: https://stringi.gagolewski.com/install.html and you are going to have to install it from your system's package manager or request its installation. I believe that it _should_ be possible because this particular package is common to many data analysis tasks, but I also know that the OSU CGRB is pretty strict with the software they allow to run on the servers (case in point, I had to do a weird workaround to get C++11 in 2016) <https://github.com/zkamvar/clonal-inference-simulations/tree/dfab4a5b61f65f777b3aa09f6188557dc331a2af#installing-on-the-cgrb-cluster-centos-66>. I wish you the best of luck.

